  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (spread): 2-up double-page spread: a text-only facing page (verso, \"Notes on the Music\", no music) on the left and the music page (recto) on the right, as ONE landscape image. The app must find the music on the right half and ignore the prose page. scan adds curl towards the gutter and 1 deg rotation; severe adds 3.5 deg rotation, perspective, aged paper (RGB). TRUTH LIMITATIONS: The facing page is prose only; its text is not part of the truth (no lyrics, no title)."
